body:
## Problem

When `HIVE_MIND_FORMAL_AI_BASE_URL` points to a separate server, Hive Mind logs and returns the **local wrapper binary's version** as `Formal AI: version …` / `runtime.formalAiVersion`. It does not query that server before assigning the version.

This prevents an operator from determining whether a just-published algorithm was actually tested, and validates the wrong binary against the minimum version.

## Evidence and exact code

All three September 4 attempts print local `0.339.1` and then use an external server:
- [Rust / Codex log](https://gist.github.com/konard/b629d7d96891b7df6705fb2d60c3cd4c), lines 191–193.
- [Kotlin / Claude log](https://gist.github.com/konard/49e0a05254e424368107a4a86ffc4d7c), lines 183–185.
- [Scala / Agent log](https://gist.github.com/konard/47115540dd330fa9a02c7fb44b8a3132), lines 315–317.

In [prepareFormalAiRuntime](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/3ed0eeff91d8d43a4056d0176374d478a49060e2/src/formal-ai-runtime.lib.mjs#L355), `readFormalAiBinaryVersion` and `assertSupportedFormalAiVersion` run on the local executable. The external-base-URL branch merely logs the URL, and the returned `formalAiVersion` remains the local value. The file is byte-identical in deployed v2.15.1 and this main revision.

The host sidecar lease code has a health probe, but that does not make the child task's version field server provenance; explicitly configured external servers also pass through this branch without a runtime server check.

**Do not conclude from these logs alone that the server was exactly 0.339.1.** That is the diagnostic ambiguity this report fixes.

## Executed reproduction

At the Hive Mind repository root, save this as `reproduce-server-version.mjs` and run `node reproduce-server-version.mjs`. It uses a real loopback HTTP server and the existing configuration seams; no hosted service is contacted.

```js
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import os from 'node:os';
import path from 'node:path';
import { createServer } from 'node:http';
import { prepareFormalAiRuntime, resetFormalAiRuntimeCache } from './src/formal-ai-runtime.lib.mjs';

const home = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'formal-ai-version-probe-'));
let requests = 0;
const server = createServer((request, response) => {
  requests++;
  response.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json');
  response.end(JSON.stringify({ version: '0.346.0', memory: { compatible: true } }));
});
await new Promise(resolve => server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve));
let runtime;
try {
  runtime = await prepareFormalAiRuntime({
    tool: 'agent', workdir: home,
    env: { HIVE_MIND_FORMAL_AI_BASE_URL: `http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`, HIVE_MIND_FORMAL_AI_HOME_ROOT: home },
    log: async message => console.log(message),
    deps: {
      readVersionImpl: async () => '0.339.1', mkdtempImpl: async () => home,
      loadRegistryImpl: async () => [{ id: 'agent', global_configs: [] }],
      seedImpl: async () => [], configureImpl: async () => {},
    },
  });
  console.log(JSON.stringify({ localWrapperVersion: '0.339.1', actualServerVersion: '0.346.0',
    reportedRuntimeVersion: runtime.formalAiVersion, serverRequests: requests }, null, 2));
  assert.equal(runtime.formalAiVersion, '0.346.0', 'remote model provenance must identify the server that answers the request');
} finally {
  await runtime?.stop();
  resetFormalAiRuntimeCache();
  await new Promise(resolve => server.close(resolve));
  fs.rmSync(home, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
```

Observed:
```json
{"localWrapperVersion":"0.339.1","actualServerVersion":"0.346.0","reportedRuntimeVersion":"0.339.1","serverRequests":0}
```

The assertion fails. The server is never queried.

## Required fix and regression coverage

- [ ] Distinguish local wrapper version from serving backend version in runtime state, ordinary logs, and attached session provenance.
- [ ] Query the actual endpoint's `/health` with a bounded deadline before client execution; validate its reported version and memory compatibility. Preserve authentication requirements.
- [ ] Carry the accepted image digest/lease version into task evidence when managed by Hive Mind. Do not infer the serving version from the wrapper or a mutable tag.
- [ ] Test local-old/server-new, local-new/server-unsupported, malformed or missing server version, unreachable endpoint, and a reused endpoint whose backend changed between tasks. Do not let runtime caching make provenance stale.
- [ ] In the three real-client replay tests, assert the recorded server version/digest is the released image actually serving those requests, then verify the source commit and remote PR diff.

The local wrapper may have a separate compatibility requirement; retain that check under its own name. This report does not request silently bypassing it.

Related reports: [update discarded on acquisition #2207](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2207), [Formal AI tool scope and argument grounding #1075](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/1075).
